      "localLabels": [
        {"name":"MEMORY_TEXT","value":261},
        {"name":"BANNER_TEXT","value":273},
        {"name":"DISP_PUT_CHAR","value":1127},
        {"name":"PRINTER_DRIVER","value":1421},
        {"name":"PRN_WAIT","value":1461},
        {"name":"CLEAR_CMD","value":7802}
      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "117": {"synopsis":"Sets up BASIC's RAM after BOOT:\n1. Copies 39 bytes from RAM_IMAGE_4080 to $4080.\n2. Writes \":\", 0 and \",\" at $41E5-$41E7 and stores $41E8 at $40A7 (the line buffer\n   PROMPT_LINE fills).\n3. Fills $4152-$41A5 with 28 jumps to $012D, which stops with error code $2C, and the 21\n   3-byte slots from $41A6 on with a RET each.\n4. Zeroes $42E8, sets SP to $41F8 and calls RESET_STACK, then CLS_CMD (display codes $1C and\n   $1F).\n5. Asks the power-on question (MEM_QUESTION) and sets the top of memory from the answer.\n6. Calls NEW_PROGRAM, prints BANNER_TEXT and goes on at BASIC_READY, BASIC's prompt.\nDoes not return."},
        "181": {"synopsis":"The power-on question: prints MEMORY_TEXT and reads the answer (PROMPT_LINE); a BREAK\n(carry) asks again. An empty answer tests RAM upwards from $434D (MEM_TEST_LOOP); a number\nsets the top itself (MEM_ANSWER). Both go on at MEM_TOP_SET.\nObserved: NEW LINE alone on the /64 (48K) made the top $FFFF."},
        "255": {"comment":"Print BANNER_TEXT: clear the screen, the version"},
        "261": {"synopsis":"The /64's power-on question, \"MEMORY SIZE\" and a zero that ends it, where Series I has\n\"READY \"; MEM_QUESTION prints it and PROMPT_LINE adds \"? \".\nObserved: the /64 shows MEMORY SIZE? at power-on."},
        "273": {"synopsis":"Printed once memory is set up, where Series I prints 27 new lines: $1C (home) and $1F\n(clear to the end of the screen) for DISPLAY_DRIVER, \"BASIC  2.20 \", two new lines and a\nzero that ends it.\nObserved: after the question the screen holds BASIC  2.20 above READY."},
        "290": {"synopsis":"Eleven zero bytes after the banner; nothing reads them."},
        "1112": {"synopsis":"The display's driver (the block at $401D: bytes 3-4 the cursor's address in $3C00-$3FFF,\nbyte 5 the character under the cursor, 0 when the cursor is not shown).\n1. Input (carry from DEV_DISPATCH): DISP_READ gives the character at the cursor.\n2. Output: puts back the character under the cursor, then by the code in C: $00-$1F control\n   codes (DISP_CONTROL); $20-$7F stored as they are, lower case included (the /64\n   has no fold to $00-$1F: NOPs at $0471-$047C); $80-$BF graphics, stored as they are; $C0-$FF n - $C0 spaces. Stepping\n   past $3FFF scrolls the screen up a row (DISP_STORE). Then DISP_CURSOR shows the cursor\n   again ($5F) and stores its address.\nEntry: IX = the block, C = the character, carry set for input.\nExit: A = the character sent (output).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "1127": {"synopsis":"DISPLAY_DRIVER: sorts the character in C by its range; on the /64, $20-$7F go straight on to\nDISP_WRITE.\nObserved: the /64's banner is stored as $42 $41 $53 (\"BAS\") where Series I stores READY as\n$12 $05 $01.","comment":"The character"},
        "1128": {"comment":"Below $20: a control code"},
        "1133": {"comment":"$80 or more: graphics or spaces"},
        "1137": {"comment":"Twelve NOPs where Series I folds $40-$7F to $00-$1F"},
        "1421": {"synopsis":"The printer's driver, without Series I's paging: by the character in C:\n- 0: the status (PRN_STATUS), Z when ready.\n- Anything else: waits until the printer is ready and writes it to port $FD (PRN_CHAR).\nThe block's bytes 3-4 (lines per page, lines printed) are not used.\nEntry: IX = the block, C = the character.\nExit: A = the character.\nChanges: AF.\nObserved: LPRINT \"X\" completes on the /64.","comment":"The character"},
        "1423": {"comment":"0: the status"},
        "1425": {"comment":"Anything else: write it"},
        "1427": {"synopsis":"33 $FF bytes where Series I has its form feed code; nothing reaches them."},
        "1460": {"synopsis":"PRINTER_DRIVER: writes the character when the printer is ready."},
        "1461": {"synopsis":"Waits until PRN_STATUS reports the printer ready.","comment":"Ready?"},
        "1466": {"comment":"The character"},
        "1468": {"comment":"To the printer"},
        "1470": {"comment":"Done: the /64 counts no lines"},
        "1471": {"synopsis":"18 $FF bytes where Series I counts the printed lines; nothing reaches them."},
        "7802": {"synopsis":"The CLEAR statement. Without an argument it clears the variables (CLEAR_VARS). With one, n,\nthe string space becomes n bytes below the top of memory ($40B1): the new bottom goes to\n$40A0 and the variables are cleared.\nn is read with EVAL_INT, where Series I uses EVAL_INT_POS: a negative n is not refused with FC\nbut taken as 65536 + n, which is too large.\nStops with error code 12 (report OM) when n is larger than the top, or the new bottom is not\nmore than 40 bytes above the program's end ($40F9).\nEntry: HL = the text after the keyword, Z set when nothing follows.\nObserved: CLEAR -1 stops with OM on the /64 and with FC on Series I.","comment":"No argument: just clear the variables"},
        "7805": {"comment":"DE = the size (EVAL_INT: no sign check)"},
        "7808": {"comment":"Anything after it? Return for the loop to report"},
        "7812": {"comment":"DE = the top of memory - the size"},
        "7821": {"comment":"Larger than the top: report OM"},
        "7824": {"comment":"HL = the program's end + 40"},
        "7831": {"comment":"Is the new bottom not above it? Report OM"},
        "7835": {"comment":"$40A0 = the string space's new bottom"},
        "7840": {"comment":"Clear the variables"}
      }
    }
  },
